      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# BirdJournal · Klein 4B distilled · telephoto scene\n\nFrom the glasses' wide lens a finch is the size of a leaf. This takes a 10–15× \"telephoto\" frame out of the full-resolution glasses photo, around a spot where a bird could perch. Cropping keeps the perspective a long lens would have from the same spot; only the depth of field is missing, so the crop is blurred into the bokeh of a 300 mm lens wide open. Klein then puts the reference bird, sharp, on a perch that belongs to the place. About 7 s a painting.\n\n**1 · The place**: `birdjournal-glasses-<lawn|garden|driveway>-3024` is the whole glasses photo (3024 × 4032). In **crop**, width and height set the zoom, and x and y set the frame's top-left corner in the photo's pixels:\n\n| zoom | width | height |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 10x | 302 | 403 |\n| 12x | 252 | 336 |\n| 15x | 202 | 269 |\n\nThe audition's spots at 12×:\n\n| spot | photo | x | y |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| lawn-lilies | `birdjournal-glasses-lawn-3024` | 674 | 1838 |\n| lawn-leaves | `birdjournal-glasses-lawn-3024` | 674 | 2158 |\n| lawn-roses | `birdjournal-glasses-lawn-3024` | 2234 | 803 |\n| lawn-branch | `birdjournal-glasses-lawn-3024` | 994 | 230 |\n| garden-lamp | `birdjournal-glasses-garden-3024` | 2226 | 230 |\n| garden-flowers | `birdjournal-glasses-garden-3024` | 1194 | 1478 |\n| garden-hedge | `birdjournal-glasses-garden-3024` | 314 | 1394 |\n| driveway-roses | `birdjournal-glasses-driveway-3024` | 2614 | 1430 |\n| driveway-shrub | `birdjournal-glasses-driveway-3024` | 1279 | 1091 |\n\n**crop (sharp)** previews the frame; **image 2 (blurred)** is what Klein sees. The blur's sigma sets the bokeh: 10 is the audition's, and 4–6 keeps more of the place (leave the radius at 31). Keep width:height at 3:4, or the scale crops the middle.\n\n**2 · The bird**: `birdjournal-bird-<species>`, cut out onto white. For the House Finch use `-bright` (brightened, with the twig scraps around its feet removed). The plain one is so dark that the model paints its own idea of the colours.\n\n**3 · Prompt and seed**: the audition's prompt. The seed picks the perch and the pose: one seed with one prompt gave the same diagonal log in every scene, so change it to see others. It is fixed so that a tweak compares with the last picture.\n\n**4 · Model**: FLUX.2 [klein] 4B distilled (fp8), 4 steps at cfg 1, so there is no negative prompt. The VAE is BFL's small decoder, and the text encoder is `qwen_3_4b`. All are Apache 2.0. Don't let the missing-model dialog fetch `flux2-vae.safetensors` (FLUX non-commercial).\n\nPaintings save to `output/birdjournal-telephoto/`. The audition's sheets are on the Mac in `build/art-bakeoff/telephoto/`."
      ],
      "title": "BirdJournal: read me",
      "color": "#232",
      "bgcolor": "#353"
    },
