      "widgets_values": [
        "Image 1 is the authoritative reference for the bird's identity. Image 2 is the background: a telephoto view of a real place, out of focus. Place this exact bird near the centre, large in the frame, about two fifths of its height, perched on something that belongs to the place in image 2: a twig or stem of its plants, the top of its hedge or shrub, a rail, a post or the ground, never a bare log, the bird and its perch in crisp focus in front of image 2's soft, creamy bokeh, which keeps its colours, light and shapes. Preserve its beak shape, eye ring, head markings, wing bars, feather pattern, tail shape, and body proportions. Adapt illumination and shadows to the scene while retaining its identifying plumage pattern. Its feet grip the perch naturally, with contact shadows. A wildlife photograph taken with a 300 mm lens wide open, convincing and physically coherent."
      ],
